<title>SINGAPORE: Broadway first half net plunges 89 pct.</title>
<headline>Broadway first half net plunges 89 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    0.05   vs    0.47</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   0.05   vs    0.41</p>
<p>    Turnover			     25.93   vs   23.67</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     0.04   vs    0.06</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  0.64   vs    0.45</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    1.91   vs    1.47</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	   0.50   vs    0.07</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			0.20   vs    0.71</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.31   vs    0.23</p>
<p>    Minorities	     (gain)     0.16   vs    0.01  (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Broadway Industrial Group Ltd said it had changed the financial year end of its associated companies to coincide with the end of its own financial year.</p>
<p>It said it received Singapore $322,000 net of tax in the six months to June 30, 1996, from its associates relating to prior financial years.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
